    "cost_per_1000_usd": "cost per 1,000 cases = mean(Drex recorded cost_usd + routed DeepInfra cost) * 1000. Routed cost is 0 when no question is sent. Otherwise it is the recorded packed call, scaled as (list input dollars + list output dollars * routed/asked) * (recorded cost_usd / list-price of that call) when cost_basis is provider_estimated_cost and both the recorded cost and the list price are positive. List rates are DeepInfra's published cents_per_token figures from _deepinfra_list. If the provider did not send estimated_cost, the scale is 1 and the list rate is used. If no list rate is known, the recorded cost_usd is scaled by routed/asked. The escalation model alone uses mean(recorded cost_usd) * 1000 and no Drex cost. Drex alone uses mean(recorded Drex cost_usd) * 1000 and no DeepInfra cost. On prior auth, a case with any routed question takes the escalation model's recorded decision and the other case-level parts; Drex keeps those when nothing is routed.",
    "latency_p50_ms": "p50 latency is the median over paired cases of [Drex recorded latency_ms + DeepInfra recorded latency_ms * routed/asked when any question is routed]. Drex alone is the median Drex latency. The escalation model alone is the median of its recorded latency."
